  "release_link_workaround": {
    "scope": "The first canonical candidate passed compile, nm and signing but dyld rejected its misaligned LINKEDIT string pool before app entry. An owned minimal cdylib reproduced the failure with Rust post-link stripping and loaded with linker-time stripping at identical file size. The FFI release package now disables Rust post-link strip; its macOS release build script asks the linker to remove local/debug symbols. Codegen units, optimization, runtime behavior, CLI/MCP profiles are unchanged. The FFI package strip override also leaves non-macOS FFI symbols unstripped; this macOS bridge has no validated non-macOS shipping artifact.",
    "reference": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/157750",
    "original_failed_app_receipt_sha256": "1be4a3b2a6c2455e1834ff1495071891fc4d64fe6e7216c2f16f1779e9f0932d",
    "minimal_fixture_receipt_sha256": "d97a1bf368113bb5c4ee971cab37b6842819b26d2c8815be2a1353a8f8806ebc"
  },
  "retained_failures_and_corrections": [
    "The first child observer divided a PID count as if it were a byte count. Its empty child-count result is invalid. Calibration against an owned known child established count semantics; corrected matched-map capture observed at least ten codesign children. Original capture remains retained; phase values are unaffected.",
    "An isolated native prototype treated CFNumberGetValue as an integer; the locked binding returns bool. A second prototype eagerly constructed a null CF owner via then_some and trapped on a missing path. The integrated implementation explicitly rejects null before constructing an owner; invalid/null/error cases pass focused and normal release tests. Neither faulty prototype was adopted.",
    "copy2 attempted to preserve protected source file flags in an owned fixture; fixed by copying bytes with an explicit executable mode. No system binary was modified.",
    "A private demangler assumption failed because the expected archive was absent; native c++filt handled legacy symbols after Mach-O underscore removal. The original link map contains invalid UTF-8 symbol bytes; preserve raw bytes and decode only a derived inspection view."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The engine already caches signing verdicts. Resolver gains apply only to uncached paths, not steady cached state or universal app CPU.",
    "Diagnostic resolver uses exact integrated source and real locked model/CF archives with opt3/codegen1/LTO-off, not a matched production-profile binary comparison. Canonical app validation uses the normal shipping pipeline.",
    "Resolver total CPU includes parent and reaped codesign children; parent CPU rises. Kernel peak self/child RSS are separate largest-process maxima, cannot be added or subtracted as aggregate app footprint. Self RSS rises in this probe.",
    "App native counters cover only the app process; excluded codesign children and Security/XPC services prevent a total-host energy or memory claim. Live host inputs drift across the four exploratory windows.",
    "Normal validation/build costs are absolute runs with warm dependencies and one Cargo job, not evidence of a compiler speedup.",
    "The prior pass ran 373 active four-root release cases; this pass runs the final-source 72 core cases, strict core all-target Clippy, formatting, canonical caller builds and retained app comparison. Do not attribute prior wider coverage to the final source.",
    "No install, merge or release. Hosted checks are verified separately at the pushed commit; local success does not override dependency-policy failures."
  ],
